ing Minh about you. The retelling is already better than the event."},{"seq":342,"day":4,"line":"Ruth showed Daniela the Sassafras — \"remember it.\" Word gets around."},{"seq":343,"day":4,"line":"Ruth showed A man, maybe 60s the Lamb's Quarters — \"remember it.\" The haven hears about it by supper."},{"seq":344,"day":4,"line":"💧 Oscar returns with water: +3 clean."},{"seq":345,"day":4,"line":"💧 A person, maybe 50s returns with water: +3 clean."},{"seq":346,"day":4,"line":"You catch A man, maybe 50s telling the fire about Otto. \"Otto taught Minh the low succulent mat, reddish stems, paddle-shaped leaves\" The story's already growing."},{"seq":347,"day":4,"line":"Otto is stitching a tear shut by the door light, squinting at every stitch."},{"seq":348,"day":4,"line":"🧳 A traveler passed through yesterday, talking about a village to the southeast called Stonebridge. The region is bigger than your fire."},{"seq":349,"day":4,"line":"A cold snap. Breath smokes. The woods go quiet."},{"seq":350,"day":4,"line":"⚠ STARVING: health and energy falling. The spiral has started."},{"seq":351,"day":4,"line":"Village meal: +1100 kcal, +1L water from the communal pantry. (Half ration — they don't trust you yet.)"},{"seq":352,"day":4,"line":"A woman, maybe 20s has been asking about the strange leaves all week — \"but what IS it?\" Tonight, an answer. A person, maybe 50s is showing everyone Lamb's Quarters by the fire. \"See the leaves? Like that. Don't mix it up.\" The journal grows — the human way."},{"seq":353,"day":4,"line":"A man, maybe 50s spends the afternoon with the tree with lobed leaves and oval nuts in scaly caps — look, smell, the smallest taste, then waiting. Raw, it knots the stomach. Cooked... fine. The fire learns the rule before the name: cook it, or else."},{"seq":354,"day":4,"line":"From the lumped bag: White Oak Acorns — named, and out."},{"seq":355,"day":4,"line":"★ IDENTIFIED: White Oak Acorns. White oak acorn. Lobed leaves, sweet acorns. Uses unknown — harvest, taste, and learn."},{"seq":356,"day":4,"line":"💡 White Oak Acorns. The tree with lobed leaves and oval nuts in scaly caps you've been looking at for days finally has a name, and now you'll never unsee it."},{"seq":357,"day":4,"line":"The Journal notes it: White Oak Acorns — cook it, or else. (A man, maybe 50s tested it.)"},{"seq":358,"day":4,"line":"🔍 A crouches over floating rosettes of leaves; under them, black horned nuts, studying it a moment before moving on. (2/3 looks)"},{"seq":359,"day":4,"line":"A woman, maybe 20s traded something with someone for something else. The barter economy stirs."},{"seq":360,"day":4,"line":"🤢 Daniela's stomach knots — something in their meal was off."},{"seq":361,"day":4,"line":"🤢 Ruth's stomach knots — something in their meal was off."},{"seq":362,"day":4,"line":"🍽️ Caleb leaves the surplus by the fire for whoever's hungry. \"The pantry can't take it. We can.\""},{"seq":363,"day":4,"line":"📓 Journal: Minh taught the man in his 50s The Forager’s Eye."},{"seq":364,"day":4,"line":"🛟 Otto stands up by the fire. \"The sick can't wait us out. Somebody has to say it, so: we need a plan, tonight. Here's what we CAN do — pick one, maybe two, but everything costs something.\""},{"seq":365,"day":4,"line":"\"Triage tents and broth for the sick, or half rations till it passes, or the healthy hunt hard to keep everyone fed. Pick — everything costs.\""},{"seq":366,"day":4,"line":"\"Or we rally,\" Otto adds. \"Second shift, everybody. We work, we eat, we live — and we pay for it.\""},{"seq":367,"day":4,"line":"(Relief is open — triage, rations, hunt, or rally, from the beats row. Each option works once; the moment passes in ~3 days.)"},{"seq":368,"day":4,"line":"📓 Journal: Otto proposed relief (sickness), day 4."},{"seq":369,"day":4,"line":"You've started noticing: Daniela and Ruth never speak. It's not new. (Something old lives in Haven.)"},{"seq":370,"day":5,"line":"— DAY 5 DAWN — The world wakes. Animals are active."},{"seq":371,"day":5,"line":"Overnight, unknown nuts; Lamb's Quarters went bad — beyond saving. You leave them for the flies."},{"seq":372,"day":5,"line":"Fresh food keeps days, not weeks. Smoke it over a fire to make it last."},{"seq":373,"day":5,"line":"The fire burns low. One new line in the journal: White Oak Acorns — named and noted."},{"seq":374,"day":5,"line":"Snow by morning. Your breath comes out in ghosts."},{"seq":375,"day":5,"line":"Hunger gnaws. The pack is thin — work the green, haul it back, get it named at camp. That's the whole game."},{"seq":376,"day":5,"line":"Dawn. You wake rested. (+18 health, energy restored. By the fire. Good enough.)"},{"seq":377,"day":5,"line":"You are full enough."},{"seq":378,"day":5,"line":"The pantry is in the hall. Your hands are not."},{"seq":379,"day":5,"line":"No risky water to boil."},{"seq":380,"day":5,"line":"Drank clean water."},{"seq":381,"day":5,"line":"📋 Otto — 💧 Fetch water. They'll report back by next part."},{"seq":382,"day":5,"line":"🌱 Caleb waters and weeds the beds before taking up other work. The harvest can wait."},{"seq":383,"day":5,"line":"🌿 Caleb checks the pantry before heading out — the shelves are full, ~6 days of fresh on hand… leaves the harvest standing and turns to the stone pile instead. The pantry can't take more; the wild will keep."},{"seq":384,"day":5,"line":"🪨 Caleb pries 1 stone loose from the creek bed. The building pile grows. (3 stone now.)"},{"seq":385,"day":5,"line":"💧 Otto returns with 10L of creek water. Risky until the hearth boils it."},{"seq":386,"day":5,"line":"You catch fragments by the fire — Otto telling Daniela about you. It's picking up decorations as it travels."},{"seq":387,"day":5,"line":"Anh showed Otto the Sassafras — \"remember it.\" Word travels before the lesson cools."},{"seq":388,"day":5,"line":"Anh showed Oscar the White Oak Acorns — \"remember it.\" Word gets around."},{"seq":389,"day":5,"line":"Minh heads out for water. \"Fetching water. Somebody has to.\""},{"seq":390,"day":5,"line":"💧 Daniela returns with water: +2 clean."},{"seq":391,"day":5,"line":"💧 Ruth returns with water: +2 clean."},{"seq":392,"day":5,"line":"Caleb heads out for water. \"Thirst doesn't negotiate. Going.\""},{"seq":393,"day":5,"line":"A woman, maybe 20s heads out for water. \"The well won't fill itself.\""},{"seq":394,"day":5,"line":"💧 A woman, maybe 30s returns with water: +2 clean."},{"seq":395,"day":5,"line":"Iron cold. Even the ticks are shelved."},{"seq":396,"day":5,"line":"— MIDDAY — Honest work hours. Heat builds."},{"seq":397,"day":5,"line":"You wait. The light changes. Nothing asks anything of you."},{"seq":398,"day":5,"line":"📋 Otto — 💧 Fetch water. They'll report back by next part."},{"seq":399,"day":5,"line":"The stash count is off. 2 stones missing. Nobody saw anything. Everybody suspects something."},{"seq":400,"day":5,"line":"The stash count is off. 1 stone missing. Nobody saw anything. Everybody suspects something."},{"seq":401,"day":5,"line":"💧 Otto eyes the cistern — full to the brim. No sense hauling water there's no room for; they turn to the stone pile instead."},{"seq":402,"day":5,"line":"🪨 Otto pries 1 stone loose from the creek bed. The building pile grows. (1 stone now.)"},{"seq":403,"day":5,"line":"A person, maybe 50s heads out for water. \"Water first. Everything else waits.\""},{"seq":404,"day":5,"line":"— DUSK — Animals stir again. Shadows lengthen."},{"seq":405,"day":5,"line":"You wait. The light changes. Nothing asks anything of you."},{"seq":406,"day":5,"line":"Otto hesitates, then backs off. \"Not today. Sorry.\" (Low trust — reluctant.)"},{"seq":407,"day":5,"line":"A person, maybe 50s showed A man, maybe 50s the Sassafras — \"remember it.\" The haven hears about it by supper."},{"seq":408,"day":5,"line":"💧 Minh returns with water: +3 clean."},{"seq":409,"day":5,"line":"💧 Caleb returns with water: +4 clean."},{"seq":410,"day":5,"line":"A man, maybe 60s heads out to forage. \"There's food out there. Going to find it.\""},{"seq":411,"day":5,"line":"💧 A woman, maybe 20s returns with water: +2 clean."},{"seq":412,"day":5,"line":"— NIGHT — Camp. Rest — or risk the dark."},{"seq":413,"day":5,"line":"Night. The treeline is just a sound now. The fire is the whole argument against it."},{"seq":414,"day":5,"line":"You wait. The light changes. Nothing asks anything of you."},{"seq":415,"day":5,"line":"Travel 2 tiles to wetland.\n— Still water, cattails —\nStanding water, black as tea. Dragonflies stitch the air. Watch where you step — the ground lies."},{"seq":416,"day":5,"line":"You see smoke on the horizon. Stonebridge — 8 people, 5 days in. fishing folk, by the look of it. They know 2 plants — 2 new to you. They've been here the whole time."},{"seq":417,"day":5,"line":"You see smoke on the horizon. Thornfield — 8 people, 5 days in. fishing folk, by the look of it. They know 2 plants — 2 new to you. They've been here the whole time."},{"seq":418,"day":5,"line":"You see smoke on the horizon. Ashford — 9 people, 5 days in. fishing folk, by the look of it. They know 4 plants — 4 new to you. They've been here the whole time."},{"seq":419,"day":5,"line":"📖 LEARNED: Old World Caches (Level 1). You know where people hid things: under floorboards, in hollow trees, behind loose bricks."},{"seq":420,"day":5,"line":"You've learned Old World Caches — it carries Eagle Eye."},{"seq":421,"day":5,"line":"Travel 1 tile to forest floor.\n— Under the canopy —\nOld growth. The canopy closes overhead and the light comes down in shafts. Something rustled, and decided not to be seen."},{"seq":422,"day":5,"line":"Travel 2 tiles to forest floor.\n— Under the canopy —\nMushrooms thumb up through the duff in a ring — a fairy ring, old as the path. You step around it, not through it. Some rules are older than knowledge."},{"seq":423,"day":5,"line":"Travel 1 tile to forest floor.\n— Under the canopy —\nMushrooms thumb up through the duff in a ring — a fairy ring, old as the path. You step around it, not through it. Some rules are older than knowledge."},{"seq":424,"day":5,"line":"You see smoke on the horizon. Emberhold — 11 people, 5 days in. fishing folk, by the look of it. They know 2 plants — 2 new to you. They've been here the whole time."},{"seq":425,"day":5,"line":"Travel 2 tiles to forest floor.\n— Under the canopy —\nSaplings push up through last year's deadfall, racing each other for the light. The forest never stops trying."},{"seq":426,"day":5,"line":"Something moves out there — the absence of sound, shaped like wings."},{"seq":427,"day":5,"line":"The creek runs fast here — no crossing without a bridge or a swim."},{"seq":428,"day":5,"line":"The creek runs fast here — no crossing without a bridge or a swim."},{"seq":429,"day":5,"line":"Travel 1 tile to thicket.\n— Thick brush —\nThe brush closes behind you like water. You learn to move sideways, leading with a shoulder."},{"seq":430,"day":5,"line":"Unfamiliar unknown berries — into the bag. (Unknowns lump together; sort them at camp.)"},{"seq":431,"day":5,"line":"You also take some vine (crafting material)."},{"seq":432,"day":5,"line":"You also take some vine (crafting material)."},{"seq":433,"day":5,"line":"Journal: Edge habitat. Berries grow where the light gets in."},{"seq":434,"day":5,"line":"A shot in the dark — you take what's green: 4× unknown berries. Into the bag, unnamed. (Not food until identified — sort them at camp.) This patch is picked clean — it'll recover in a few days."},{"seq":435,"day":5,"line":"Travel 1 tile to forest floor."},{"seq":436,"day":5,"line":"The Snare comes apart in your hands. The materials are wasted. (craft failed)"},{"seq":437,"day":5,"line":"...and then it lands: A person, maybe 50s speaks 🇺🇸 English. A few shared words. Gestures. Patience."},{"seq":438,"day":5,"line":"\"Adil,\" they say, touching their chest. \"I'm Adil.\" You'll remember that."},{"seq":439,"day":5,"line":"📓 Journal: learned their name (Adil)."},{"seq":440,"day":5,"line":"Nothing edible. (unknown berries — not food yet: identify it first — test cautiously from your pack, or sort it at camp.)"},{"seq":441,"day":5,"line":"Sleeping rough means the cold ground — heal ~16. Cold snap — sleeping exposed will hurt you. Find shelter or build a fire. Tonight will cost you — the night burns ~2200 kcal and you haven't eaten enough today. Eat and drink before you sleep, or the spiral starts at midnight."},{"seq":442,"day":5,"line":"You settle into the cold ground. Sleep takes you."},{"seq":443,"day":5,"line":"The stash count is off. 1 stone missing. Nobody saw anything. Everybody suspects something."},{"seq":444,"day":5,"line":"Daniela doesn't bother arguing anymore. By dusk the Fish crews are taking orders from them, and nobody quite remembers when it changed."},{"seq":445,"day":5,"line":"🧳 A traveler passed through yesterday, talking about a village to the northeast called Ashford. The region is bigger than your fire."},{"seq":446,"day":5,"line":"A cold snap. Breath smokes. The woods go quiet."},{"seq":447,"day":5,"line":"⚠ STARVING: health and energy falling. The spiral has started."},{"seq":448,"day":5,"line":"You camp wild tonight — no pantry meal. Eat from your pack."},{"seq":449,"day":5,"line":"🍽️ Minh sets the sharing basket down by the fire instead of the pantry. \"Full shelves don't need my little more.\""},{"seq":450,"day":5,"line":"📓 Journal: Minh taught Oscar Camp Cooking."},{"seq":451,"day":5,"line":"🤒 Daniela made it through the worst of it — the fever finally broke."},{"seq":452,"day":5,"line":"Fresh-cut stems on the northeast ground — someone else is working turf your crews use. (Emberhold's foragers, most likely. You walk the ground yourself: it's thinner than your crews alone could strip it.)"},{"seq":453,"day":5,"line":"Fresh-cut stems on the southeast ground — someone else is working turf your crews use. (Stonebridge's foragers, most likely. You walk the ground yourself: it's thinner than your crews alone could strip it.)"},{"seq":454,"day":5,"line":"Fresh-cut stems on the northeast ground — someone else is working turf your crews use. (Thornfield's foragers, most likely. You walk the ground yourself: it's thinner than your crews alone could strip it.)"},{"seq":455,"day":5,"line":"Fresh-cut stems on the northeast ground — someone else is working turf your crews use. (Ashford's foragers, most likely. You walk the ground yourself: it's thinner than your crews alone could strip it.)"},{"seq":456,"day":6,"line":"— DAY 6 DAWN — The world wakes. Animals are active."},{"seq":457,"day":6,"line":"👀 Someone mentioned Denver and Ruth answered to it a beat late — like responding to a name that isn't quite yours."},{"seq":458,"day":6,"line":"📓 Journal: jotted down what they said (Ruth)."},{"seq":459,"day":6,"line":"Snow by morning. Your breath comes out in ghosts."},{"seq":460,"day":6,"line":"Your stomach is a fist. Eat — anything real, now."},{"seq":461,"day":6,"line":"Dawn. You wake stiff and half-frozen. (-23 health, restless night. Your sleeping body burned less — 309 kcal conserved. The cold got in — no healing, and it took its cut. (Sleeping unsheltered in a cold snap is a mistake you only make once.))"},{"seq":462,"day":6,"line":"Nothing edible. (unknown berries — not food yet: identify it first — test cautiously from your pack, or sort it at camp.)"},{"seq":463,"day":6,"line":"The pantry is in the hall. Your hands are not."},{"seq":464,"day":6,"line":"Need a fire to boil water."},{"seq":465,"day":6,"line":"Hunger gnaws. The pack is thin — work the green, haul it back, get it named at camp. That's the whole game."},{"seq":466,"day":6,"line":"Drank clean water."},{"seq":467,"day":6,"line":"🌱 Caleb waters and weeds the beds before taking up other work. The harvest can wait."},{"seq":468,"day":6,"line":"🌿 Caleb checks the pantry before heading out — the shelves are full, ~6 days of fresh on hand… leaves the harvest standing and turns to the wood run instead. The pantry can't take more; the wild will keep."},{"seq":469,"day":6,"line":"🪵 Caleb hauls back 5 wood. The pile grows. (33 logs now.)"},{"seq":470,"day":6,"line":"💧 Daniela returns with 7L of creek water. Risky until the hearth boils it."},{"seq":471,"day":6,"line":"The cold snap steals your warmth — breath smoking, fingers clumsy. (-20 kcal shivering. Fire, the hall, or your tent.)"},{"seq":472,"day":6,"line":"Iron cold. Even the ticks are shelved."},{"seq":473,"day":6,"line":"— MIDDAY — Honest work hours. Heat builds."},{"seq":474,"day":6,"line":"You wait. The light changes. Nothing asks anything of you."},{"seq":475,"day":6,"line":"🪨 Daniela pries 1 stone loose from the creek bed. The building pile grows. (1 stone now.)"},{"seq":476,"day":6,"line":"The cold snap steals your warmth — breath smoking, fingers clumsy. (-20 kcal shivering. Fire, the hall, or your tent.)"},{"seq":477,"day":6,"line":"— DUSK — Animals stir again. Shadows lengthen."},{"seq":478,"day":6,"line":"🌙 Something owns the night out here. You haven't learned its name yet — but the dark gets busier after sunset, and every step is riskier. A lit fire is a beacon — light through canvas, smoke on the wind. Sealed and dark, you're just a smell in the night. Haven's walls end every argument."},{"seq":479,"day":6,"line":"You wait. The light changes. Nothing asks anything of you."},{"seq":480,"day":6,"line":"🪵 Daniela hauls back 5 wood. The pile grows. (38 logs now.)"},{"seq":481,"day":6,"line":"Otto showed Oscar the Sassafras — \"remember it.\" Word travels before the lesson cools."},{"seq":482,"day":6,"line":"The cold snap steals your warmth — breath smoking, fingers clumsy. (-20 kcal shivering. Fire, the hall, or your tent.)"},{"seq":483,"day":6,"line":"— NIGHT — Camp. Rest — or risk the dark."},{"seq":484,"day":6,"line":"Night settles. The fire is the whole world now. No watches posted. The dark feels bigger than it should."},{"seq":485,"day":6,"line":"You stay up through the cold snap instead of sleeping — and the cold gets in anyway. Shivering all night, no real rest. (-12 health, energy won't rise past 40 tonight.)"},{"seq":486,"day":6,"line":"You wait. The light changes. Nothing asks anything of you."},{"seq":487,"day":6,"line":"The creek runs fast here — no crossing without a bridge or a swim."},{"seq":488,"day":6,"line":"The creek runs fast here — no crossing without a bridge or a swim."},{"seq":489,"day":6,"line":"The creek runs fast here — no crossing without a bridge or a swim."},{"seq":490,"day":6,"line":"Travel 1 tile to thicket."},{"seq":491,"day":6,"line":"You catch fragments by the fire — A woman, maybe 30s telling A man, maybe 50s about Adil. The story's getting bigger than what happened."},{"seq":492,"day":6,"line":"This patch is worked out — step to another green patch and forage again."},{"seq":493,"day":6,"line":"Travel 1 tile to thicket.\n— Thick brush —\nThe brush closes behind you like water. You learn to move sideways, leading with a shoulder."},{"seq":494,"day":6,"line":"Some of these unknown berries are starting to look familiar — sort them at camp in good light and the name might come to you."},{"seq":495,"day":6,"line":"Some of these unknown berries are starting to look familiar — sort them at camp in good light and the name might come to you."},{"seq":496,"day":6,"line":"You also take some vine (crafting material)."},{"seq":497,"day":6,"line":"Journal: Edge habitat. Berries grow where the light gets in."},{"seq":498,"day":6,"line":"A shot in the dark — you take what's green: 6× unknown berries. Into the bag, unnamed. (Not food until identified — sort them at camp.) This patch is picked clean — it'll recover in a few days."},{"seq":499,"day":6,"line":"Travel 2 tiles to forest floor."},{"seq":500,"day":6,"line":"Sleeping rough means the cold ground — heal ~16. Cold snap — sleeping exposed will hurt you. Find shelter or build a fire. Tonight will cost you — the night burns ~2200 kcal and you haven't eaten enough today. Eat and drink before you sleep, or the spiral starts at midnight."},{"seq":501,"day":6,"line":"You settle into 