 catch fragments by the fire — A man, maybe 60s, with a shaved head telling Ole about Eamon. Three retellings in, nobody remembers what actually happened — but everyone has opinions."},{"seq":160,"day":3,"line":"Eamon heads out for water. \"Water first. Everything else waits.\""},{"seq":161,"day":3,"line":"A man, maybe 60s, with tattooed arms heads out for water. \"Fetching water. Somebody has to.\""},{"seq":162,"day":3,"line":"💧 A man, maybe 30s returns with water: +4 clean."},{"seq":163,"day":3,"line":"A man, maybe 40s, with a limp heads out for water. \"The well won't fill itself.\""},{"seq":164,"day":3,"line":"A man, maybe 60s, with a shaved head heads out for water. \"Off to the well — back with a full skin.\""},{"seq":165,"day":3,"line":"Iron cold. Even the ticks are shelved."},{"seq":166,"day":3,"line":"— MIDDAY — Honest work hours. Heat builds."},{"seq":167,"day":3,"line":"You wait. The light changes. Nothing asks anything of you."},{"seq":168,"day":3,"line":"Eamon looks at you flatly. \"Why should I listen to you?\" (Trust too low.)"},{"seq":169,"day":3,"line":"👂 Overheard — Ole: \"We should eat together tonight. All of us. It matters.\""},{"seq":170,"day":3,"line":"👂 Overheard — Jesse: \"Okay — what's the first step?\""},{"seq":171,"day":3,"line":"👂 Ole \"Don't just stand there — you've got opinions, right?\""},{"seq":172,"day":3,"line":"A man, maybe 30s heads out for water. \"Thirst doesn't negotiate. Going.\""},{"seq":173,"day":3,"line":"— DUSK — Animals stir again. Shadows lengthen."},{"seq":174,"day":3,"line":"You wait. The light changes. Nothing asks anything of you."},{"seq":175,"day":3,"line":"\"You haven't earned that yet,\" Eamon says. (Trust too low.)"},{"seq":176,"day":3,"line":"A person, maybe 60s eats from the pantry."},{"seq":177,"day":3,"line":"👂 Overheard — Ole: \"Someone's been crying at night. Not naming names — just be kind today.\""},{"seq":178,"day":3,"line":"👂 Overheard — Jesse: \"Good. I'll take the first rotation. Somebody has to.\""},{"seq":179,"day":3,"line":"\"Can we talk?\" A person, maybe 60s sits down near you. \"Just... talk. Like people used to.\" (Talk to A person, maybe 60s.)"},{"seq":180,"day":3,"line":"You catch fragments by the fire — A woman, maybe 20s telling A man, maybe 50s, with a crooked nose about you. The truth left this story two fires ago. What's left is better theater."},{"seq":181,"day":3,"line":"💧 Eamon returns with water: +3 clean."},{"seq":182,"day":3,"line":"💧 A man, maybe 60s, with tattooed arms returns with water: +3 clean."},{"seq":183,"day":3,"line":"💧 A man, maybe 60s, with a shaved head returns with water: +2 clean."},{"seq":184,"day":3,"line":"— NIGHT — Camp. Rest — or risk the dark."},{"seq":185,"day":3,"line":"Night settles. The fire is the whole world now. No watches posted. The dark feels bigger than it should."},{"seq":186,"day":3,"line":"You wait. The light changes. Nothing asks anything of you."},{"seq":187,"day":3,"line":"Travel 1 tile to grove.\n— Nut trees —\nMast crunches underfoot — last season's nuts, sprouting or rotting. The trees don't waste anything."},{"seq":188,"day":3,"line":"Something big is moving in the woods. The birds went quiet."},{"seq":189,"day":3,"line":"You see smoke on the horizon. Emberhold — 12 people, 3 days in. fishing folk, by the look of it. They know 4 plants — 4 new to you. They've been here the whole time."},{"seq":190,"day":3,"line":"Unfamiliar unknown berries — into the bag. (Unknowns lump together; sort them at camp.)"},{"seq":191,"day":3,"line":"Journal: Riparian ground. Water means life, and lunch."},{"seq":192,"day":3,"line":"📓 Journal: you UNDERSTAND Green Thumb, Literally. It resonates with: something unnamed, something unnamed."},{"seq":193,"day":3,"line":"A shot in the dark — you take what's green: 7× unknown berries. Into the bag, unnamed. (Not food until identified — sort them at camp.) This patch is picked clean — it'll recover in a few days."},{"seq":194,"day":3,"line":"Travel 1 tile to Haven."},{"seq":195,"day":3,"line":"1 unprocessed haul onto the counter — the clock is ticking."},{"seq":196,"day":3,"line":"Someone by the fire nods at the counter. \"We pool food here. Keep what you need for the road — the rest feeds everyone, once it's food.\""},{"seq":197,"day":3,"line":"Nobody at the fire knows your haul any better than you do. It'll be your own hands that teach you."},{"seq":198,"day":3,"line":"You walk back into Haven. 4 Codex entries. The village is glad to see you."},{"seq":199,"day":3,"line":"A person, maybe 60s picks through the bag, frowning. Nothing they can name with confidence. (8 ticks)"},{"seq":200,"day":3,"line":"You break ground behind the hall — bed 3 of 4, turned and ready. Sow seed to start a crop."},{"seq":201,"day":3,"line":"You break ground behind the hall — bed 4 of 4, turned and ready. Sow seed to start a crop."},{"seq":202,"day":3,"line":"You catch fragments by the fire — Paolo telling Ole about Eamon. Half of it's true anymore. You're not sure which half."},{"seq":203,"day":3,"line":"A man, maybe 30s showed Eamon the Pawpaw — \"remember it.\" The haven hears about it by supper."},{"seq":204,"day":3,"line":"💧 A man, maybe 30s returns with water: +4 clean."},{"seq":205,"day":3,"line":"💧 A man, maybe 40s, with a limp returns with water: +2 clean."},{"seq":206,"day":3,"line":"⚠ STARVING: health and energy falling. You went to bed on an empty stomach."},{"seq":207,"day":3,"line":"Village meal: +1280 kcal, +1L water from the communal pantry. (Half ration — they don't trust you yet.)"},{"seq":208,"day":3,"line":"A woman, maybe 20s has been asking about the strange leaves all week — \"but what IS it?\" Tonight, an answer. Eamon is showing everyone translucent watery stems, orange-yellow trumpet flowers with spots, grows in wet shade by the fire. \"See the leaves? Like that. Don't mix it up.\" The journal grows — the human way."},{"seq":209,"day":3,"line":"Jesse spends the afternoon with the thorny bush with dark berries — look, smell, the smallest taste, then waiting. An hour passes. Then another. Nothing. The fire nods. That's dinner, maybe."},{"seq":210,"day":3,"line":"From the lumped bag: Blackberry — named, and out."},{"seq":211,"day":3,"line":"★ IDENTIFIED: Blackberry. Thorny canes, dark berries. Uses unknown — harvest, taste, and learn."},{"seq":212,"day":3,"line":"💡 You see it again in your mind: a thorny bush with dark berries. Jesse's words land on the memory like a label. Blackberry. Of course."},{"seq":213,"day":3,"line":"Paolo was watching. Now they know Blackberry too."},{"seq":214,"day":3,"line":"🔍 A crouches over broad leaves standing tall above still water on stiff stalks, studying it a moment before moving on. (1/3 looks)"},{"seq":215,"day":3,"line":"A man, maybe 30s: \"The translucent watery stems, orange-yellow trumpet flowers with spots, grows in wet shade patch is fruiting again. Somebody should get out there.\""},{"seq":216,"day":3,"line":"Paolo and Eamon lingered over the fire together."},{"seq":217,"day":3,"line":"Ole and Stanley lingered over the fire together."},{"seq":218,"day":3,"line":"Somchai and Ole lingered over the fire together."},{"seq":219,"day":3,"line":"David and Paolo lingered over the fire together."},{"seq":220,"day":3,"line":"🍽️ Nikolai looks at the full shelves and waves off the day's share. \"No more into the store — we eat at the fire, and the shelves keep.\""},{"seq":221,"day":3,"line":"📓 Journal: Paolo taught the woman in her 20s Old World Caches."},{"seq":222,"day":3,"line":"Fresh-cut stems on the northwest ground — someone else is working turf your crews use. (Emberhold's foragers, most likely. You walk the ground yourself: it's thinner than your crews alone could strip it.)"},{"seq":223,"day":4,"line":"— DAY 4 DAWN — The world wakes. Animals are active."},{"seq":224,"day":4,"line":"Overnight, unknown berries went bad — beyond saving. You leave it for the flies."},{"seq":225,"day":4,"line":"Fresh food keeps days, not weeks. Smoke it over a fire to make it last."},{"seq":226,"day":4,"line":"The fire burns low. One new line in the journal: Blackberry — named and noted."},{"seq":227,"day":4,"line":"👀 the person in their 60s was talking about home — then stopped mid-sentence, recalibrated, and said \"Denver\" just a fraction too deliberately. Whatever home is, it isn't where that sentence started."},{"seq":228,"day":4,"line":"📓 Journal: jotted down what they said (A person, maybe 60s)."},{"seq":229,"day":4,"line":"📋 Jesse — 🎣 Fish. They'll report back by next part."},{"seq":230,"day":4,"line":"📋 A person, maybe 60s — 🎣 Fish. They'll report back by next part."},{"seq":231,"day":4,"line":"You are full enough."},{"seq":232,"day":4,"line":"The pantry is in the hall. Your hands are not."},{"seq":233,"day":4,"line":"It's barely dawn. The day is yours — sleep is for later."},{"seq":234,"day":4,"line":"No risky water to boil."},{"seq":235,"day":4,"line":"Drank clean water."},{"seq":236,"day":4,"line":"Eamon shakes their head. \"Ask someone who trusts you.\" (Trust too low.)"},{"seq":237,"day":4,"line":"🌿 Jesse checks the pantry before heading out — the shelves are full, ~5 days of fresh on hand… leaves the fish nets standing and turns to the wood run instead. The pantry can't take more; the wild will keep."},{"seq":238,"day":4,"line":"🪵 Jesse hauls back 4 wood. The pile grows. (20 logs now.)"},{"seq":239,"day":4,"line":"💧 A person, maybe 60s returns with 7L of creek water. Risky until the hearth boils it."},{"seq":240,"day":4,"line":"A person, maybe 60s heads out for water. \"Fetching water. Somebody has to.\""},{"seq":241,"day":4,"line":"Eamon heads out for water. \"Thirst doesn't negotiate. Going.\""},{"seq":242,"day":4,"line":"Ole heads out for water. \"The well won't fill itself.\""},{"seq":243,"day":4,"line":"A man, maybe 30s heads out for water. \"Off to the well — back with a full skin.\""},{"seq":244,"day":4,"line":"Jesse sets out to find A person, maybe 60s. \"Won't be long.\""},{"seq":245,"day":4,"line":"A man, maybe 50s,