day":5,"line":"Drank clean water."},{"seq":332,"day":5,"line":"Eamon shakes their head. \"Ask someone who trusts you.\" (Trust too low.)"},{"seq":333,"day":5,"line":"🌿 A person, maybe 60s checks the pantry before heading out — the shelves are full, ~6 days of fresh on hand… leaves the harvest standing and turns to the water run instead. The pantry can't take more; the wild will keep."},{"seq":334,"day":5,"line":"💧 A person, maybe 60s returns with 8L of creek water. Risky until the hearth boils it."},{"seq":335,"day":5,"line":"You catch fragments by the fire — A man, maybe 50s, with a crooked nose telling Paolo about A man, maybe 30s. The details have shifted. Nobody seems to mind."},{"seq":336,"day":5,"line":"A man, maybe 30s showed A man, maybe 60s, with tattooed arms the Spicebush — \"remember it.\" Word gets around."},{"seq":337,"day":5,"line":"🩹 Eamon is still hurting (53 HP) — no healer at haven. They rest today instead of ranging out."},{"seq":338,"day":5,"line":"Paolo heads out for water. \"The well won't fill itself.\""},{"seq":339,"day":5,"line":"A man, maybe 50s, with a crooked nose heads out to forage. \"There's food out there. Going to find it.\""},{"seq":340,"day":5,"line":"Iron cold. Even the ticks are shelved."},{"seq":341,"day":5,"line":"— MIDDAY — Honest work hours. Heat builds."},{"seq":342,"day":5,"line":"You wait. The light changes. Nothing asks anything of you."},{"seq":343,"day":5,"line":"Eamon looks at you flatly. \"Why should I listen to you?\" (Trust too low.)"},{"seq":344,"day":5,"line":"You catch fragments by the fire — Eamon telling Paolo about A man, maybe 40s, with a limp. Someone's added a flourish that wasn't there this morning."},{"seq":345,"day":5,"line":"A man, maybe 30s showed Eamon the Spicebush — \"remember it.\" The haven hears about it by supper."},{"seq":346,"day":5,"line":"Ole sets out to find A man, maybe 50s, with a crooked nose. \"Won't be long.\""},{"seq":347,"day":5,"line":"A man, maybe 30s heads out for water. \"Thirst doesn't negotiate. Going.\""},{"seq":348,"day":5,"line":"— DUSK — Animals stir again. Shadows lengthen."},{"seq":349,"day":5,"line":"You wait. The light changes. Nothing asks anything of you."},{"seq":350,"day":5,"line":"Eamon shakes their head. \"Ask someone who trusts you.\" (Trust too low.)"},{"seq":351,"day":5,"line":"The stash count is off. 1 stone missing. Nobody saw anything. Everybody suspects something."},{"seq":352,"day":5,"line":"You catch fragments by the fire — A man, maybe 30s telling Jesse about A person, maybe 60s. The retelling is already better than the event."},{"seq":353,"day":5,"line":"💧 Paolo returns with water: +4 clean."},{"seq":354,"day":5,"line":"A woman, maybe 20s heads out to forage. \"Gone looking. Don't wait up.\""},{"seq":355,"day":5,"line":"Jesse heads out for water. \"Fetching water. Somebody has to.\""},{"seq":356,"day":5,"line":"— NIGHT — Camp. Rest — or risk the dark."},{"seq":357,"day":5,"line":"🔥 The fire settles. Eamon has been quiet all evening, and now everyone knows why. \"Something displaced a LOT of water, and it wasn't a log — I put it down today.\" \"The water bulges — a ripple with intent.\" \"It loosens, reluctantly, and pours itself back into the water. It will remember this pool.\" A beat of silence, then the questions come all at once. Ole says quietly \"And you're still standing."},{"seq":358,"day":5,"line":"No watches tonight. Everyone sleeps with one ear open and pretends not to."},{"seq":359,"day":5,"line":"You wait. The light changes. Nothing asks anything of you."},{"seq":360,"day":5,"line":"Travel 1 tile to grove."},{"seq":361,"day":5,"line":"This patch is worked out — step to another green patch and forage again."},{"seq":362,"day":5,"line":"Travel 2 tiles to trail edge."},{"seq":363,"day":5,"line":"Something moves out there — a raccoon with too many fingers, working at something."},{"seq":364,"day":5,"line":"This patch is worked out — step to another green patch and forage again."},{"seq":365,"day":5,"line":"The creek runs fast here — no crossing without a bridge or a swim."},{"seq":366,"day":5,"line":"Travel 1 tile to Haven."},{"seq":367,"day":5,"line":"The raccoon with too many fingers stops at the treeline — pacing, unwilling. The walls end the argument. It's still out there."},{"seq":368,"day":5,"line":"You walk back into Haven. 6 Codex entries. The village is glad to see you."},{"seq":369,"day":5,"line":"Eamon picks through the bag, frowning. Nothing they can name with confidence. (8 ticks)"},{"seq":370,"day":5,"line":"📋 Jesse — 🎣 Fish. They'll report back by next part."},{"seq":371,"day":5,"line":"📋 A person, maybe 60s — 🎣 Fish. They'll report back by next part."},{"seq":372,"day":5,"line":"...and then it lands: A man, maybe 40s, with a limp speaks 🇺🇸 English. A few shared words. Gestures. Patience."},{"seq":373,"day":5,"line":"\"David,\" they say, touching their chest. \"I'm David.\" You'll remember that."},{"seq":374,"day":5,"line":"📓 Journal: learned their name (David)."},{"seq":375,"day":5,"line":"A person, maybe 60s leans in, voice low. \"Here's what we figured out about a raccoon with too many fingers, working at something. Buy it off. It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase.\""},{"seq":376,"day":5,"line":"💡 COUNTER LEARNED — a raccoon with too many fingers, working at something: Buy it off. It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase. (Someone at the haven knew the trick.)"},{"seq":377,"day":5,"line":"📓 Journal: Counter: Buy it off — It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase."},{"seq":378,"day":5,"line":"You settle into the hall floor. Sleep takes you."},{"seq":379,"day":5,"line":"🪨 Jesse pries 1 stone loose from the creek bed. The building pile grows. (1 stone now.)"},{"seq":380,"day":5,"line":"🪵 A person, maybe 60s hauls back 4 wood. The pile grows. (26 logs now.)"},{"seq":381,"day":5,"line":"You catch fragments by the fire — A man, maybe 30s telling A man, maybe 60s, with tattooed arms about himself. It's picking up decorations as it travels."},{"seq":382,"day":5,"line":"You catch fragments by the fire — Eamon telling Jesse about A woman, maybe 20s. The story's getting bigger than what happened."},{"seq":383,"day":5,"line":"Paolo came back from the treeline white-faced. Saw it too. Whatever it is, it's still out there."},{"seq":384,"day":5,"line":"⚠ STARVING: health and energy falling. The spiral has started."},{"seq":385,"day":5,"line":"Village meal: +1000 kcal, +1L water from the communal pantry. (Half ration — they don't trust you yet.)"},{"seq":386,"day":5,"line":"Fireside lesson: A man, maybe 60s, with a shaved head passes around a thorny arching shrub hung with small oblong red berries. Someone asks a dumb question. Nobody minds. That's how you learn."},{"seq":387,"day":5,"line":"David spends the afternoon with the tree with lobed leaves and oval nuts in scaly caps — look, smell, the smallest taste, then waiting. Raw, it knots the stomach. Cooked... fine. The fire learns the rule before the name: cook it, or else."},{"seq":388,"day":5,"line":"From the lumped bag: White Oak Acorns — named, and out."},{"seq":389,"day":5,"line":"★ IDENTIFIED: White Oak Acorns. White oak acorn. Lobed leaves, sweet acorns. Uses unknown — harvest, taste, and learn."},{"seq":390,"day":5,"line":"💡 White Oak Acorns. The tree with lobed leaves and oval nuts in scaly caps you've been looking at for days finally has a name, and now you'll never unsee it."},{"seq":391,"day":5,"line":"Ole was watching. Now they know White Oak Acorns too."},{"seq":392,"day":5,"line":"The Journal notes it: White Oak Acorns — cook it, or else. (David tested it.)"},{"seq":393,"day":5,"line":"Jesse came back with 373 kcal of something edible. The pantry can't take it all — 187 kcal in, 186 kcal eaten at the fire."},{"seq":394,"day":5,"line":"David and Eamon lingered over the fire together."},{"seq":395,"day":5,"line":"🍽️ Grigory leaves the surplus by the fire for whoever's hungry. \"The pantry can't take it. We can.\""},{"seq":396,"day":5,"line":"🤒 Eamon is achy and wrung out, barely eating. Rest and clean water — or it gets worse."},{"seq":397,"day":6,"line":"— DAY 6 DAWN — The world wakes. Animals are active."},{"seq":398,"day":6,"line":"The fire burns low. One new line in the journal: White Oak Acorns — named and noted."},{"seq":399,"day":6,"line":"🔥 “I don’t say this lightly.” Stanley sets their bowl down. “Grigory, your past story isn’t true, is it? I’ve heard enough versions now.” Nobody looks at Grigory. Everybody does."},{"seq":400,"day":6,"line":"Hunger gnaws. The pack is thin — work the green, haul it back, get it named at camp. That's the whole game."},{"seq":401,"day":6,"line":"Dawn. You wake rested. (+0 health, energy restored. Your sleeping body burned less — 65 kcal conserved. By the fire. Good enough.)"},{"seq":402,"day":6,"line":"You are full enough."},{"seq":403,"day":6,"line":"The pantry is in the hall. Your hands are not."},{"seq":404,"day":6,"line":"No risky water to boil."},{"seq":405,"day":6,"line":"Drank clean water."},{"seq":406,"day":6,"line":"Eamon looks at you flatly. \"Why should I listen to you?\" (Trust too low.)"},{"seq":407,"day":6,"line":"The stash count is off. 1 stone missing. Nobody saw anything. Everybody suspects something."},{"seq":408,"day":6,"line":"🌿 A person, maybe 60s checks the pantry before heading out — the shelves are full, ~7 days of fresh on hand… leaves the harvest standing and turns to the water run instead. The pantry can't take more; the wild will keep."},{"seq":409,"day":6,"line":"💧 A person, maybe 60s returns with 10L of creek water. Risky until the hearth boils it."},{"seq":410,"day":6,"line":"